{
  "id": "COMPOUND:20723 - PROTEIN:1642",
  "verbalization": "The compound in question, a complex oxan-4-yl derivative, is implicated in the activation of Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src through multiple indirect pathways. It is directly linked to RAF proto-oncogene serine/threonine-protein kinase, which is a well-known downstream target of the RAS signaling pathway. This connection is further supported by the fact that RAF is also a target of (6Z,10E,14Z,18E)-2,6,10,15,19,23-hexamethyltetracosa-2,6,10,14,18,22-hexaene, a compound that is itself a target of trans-Norbixin. Trans-Norbixin is a known inhibitor of Src, suggesting a potential mechanism by which this compound may influence Src activity. Additionally, the compound is linked to Coagulation factor VII, which is a target of trans-Norbixin, reinforcing the possibility of a broader signaling network involving Src. These findings collectively suggest that the compound may act through a complex, multi-tiered mechanism involving the RAS pathway and Src, potentially through interactions with RAF and other downstream targets.",
